# Far copy, step 26.3 (7.2.44): the asker. One program of language 3, nothing new: data, emit, key, warn, goto, halt. It sends the requests by hand
# (the record of far_serve.tw: op, pos, dat, 3 bytes, every one by `emit`), puts every answer (`key`) into its own cell g1..g6
# and at the end sends op = 0 and prints the cells to stderr. Its stdout must go to the stdin of far_serve.tw and its stdin must be
# the stdout of far_serve.tw. A cell starts as all ones (the prohibitive price): if the channel is closed (EOF) a read leaves it as it
# was, so "no answer" is the same as the answer "no such cell"; if the answerer is alive but silent, the read waits (no tick passes).
# Rows of different devices are not ordered by the layout (no data connects an `emit` and a `key`: the packing puts the `key` into
# the first layer, before the later `emit`s of its block, and the asker would wait for an answer to a request not yet sent: a deadlock).
# So every `key` is a block of its own (the `goto` before it is a tick boundary): the writes of the block before it are done.
# The requests: get 2, get 5, put 3 <- 165, get 3, get 8 (outside the window), put 9 <- 77 (outside: nothing changes), get 1, get 200.
:opget data 8 1
:opput data 8 2
:opstop data 8 0
:p1 data 8 1
:p2 data 8 2
:p3 data 8 3
:p5 data 8 5
:p8 data 8 8
:p9 data 8 9
:p200 data 8 200
:d0 data 8 0
:d77 data 8 77
:d165 data 8 165
:g1 data 8 255
:g2 data 8 255
:g3 data 8 255
:g4 data 8 255
:g5 data 8 255
:g6 data 8 255
:main block
goto &q1
:q1 block
emit &opget
emit &p2
emit &d0
goto &a1
:a1 block
key &g1
goto &q2
:q2 block
emit &opget
emit &p5
emit &d0
goto &a2
:a2 block
key &g2
goto &q3
:q3 block
emit &opput
emit &p3
emit &d165
goto &q4
:q4 block
emit &opget
emit &p3
emit &d0
goto &a4
:a4 block
key &g3
goto &q5
:q5 block
emit &opget
emit &p8
emit &d0
goto &a5
:a5 block
key &g4
goto &q6
:q6 block
emit &opput
emit &p9
emit &d77
goto &q7
:q7 block
emit &opget
emit &p1
emit &d0
goto &a7
:a7 block
key &g5
goto &q8
:q8 block
emit &opget
emit &p200
emit &d0
goto &a8
:a8 block
key &g6
goto &stop
:stop block
emit &opstop
emit &d0
emit &d0
goto &show
:show block
warn &g1
warn &g2
warn &g3
warn &g4
warn &g5
warn &g6
halt
